{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The proposed relation is 'contradiction', but the content concedes that SRC_003's demand is for population statistics while the isolated node relies on a single-run ablation. Those positions are not logically incompatible: a single-run procedural criterion can be insufficient in general yet still constitute one defeasible source of evidence, so the two claims can both hold without contradiction. What is presented is a contrast between evidential standards, not a genuine contradiction relation. The REFUTED IF clause only rescinds the contradiction after the fact by showing the ablation lacks power and thereby vindicates SRC_003; it does not establish that the original contradiction relation was substantive — it exposes that the endpoints are compatible (a difference in sufficiency thresholds) rather than contradictory.","counterexample":["Let A = 'single-run criteria do not suffice for genuine verification' (SRC_003).","Let B = 'this single-run perturbation-sensitivity ablation yields a causal mechanism sufficient to distinguish genuine verification from restatement' (isolated node).","Under a defeasible reading where B is one instance of single-run evidence, A and B can both be true if B is merely a sufficient diagnostic in its limited domain and not a claim that all single-run criteria suffice; hence no logical contradiction obtains."],"target":"67bd081f1eed8f9a1ba2a816a0aefd74b978fb2344a4f3462c5a4baf81b528d0"}]}